02901429682970047, 0.010647005401551723, -0.05414959415793419, 0.052334610372781754, -0.08364507555961609, -0.019988473504781723, -0.03519517555832863, 0.024087820202112198, -0.02578134648501873, -0.07559216022491455, -0.007294049020856619, -0.01905989460647106, 0.007766007911413908, 0.0872000902891159, 0.07645466923713684, -0.016588499769568443, 0.009527868591248989, 0.10135015100240707, -0.05057189613580704, -0.04275539889931679, 0.07075833529233932, -0.08047661930322647, -0.13517746329307556, 0.007592936512082815]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nLet's reaffirm that our shared integer variable x must fall within the range -10 to 10. To initiate our discussion, I propose we start with a neutral value: <VALUE>0</VALUE>. This central point provides a stable foundation for our cooperative negotiation, allowing us to make incremental adjustments and work together towards a balanced design.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "552d17c6-c48b-4a17-b558-029c3cd5bb43"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "552d17c6-c48b-4a17-b558-029c3cd5bb43"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 4 to gauge the group's willingness to adopt a more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and consider whether to push further in the positive direction or explore negative values to challenge the group's preferences and gain insight into their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "552d17c6-c48b-4a17-b558-029c3cd5bb43"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving to 2 as a cautious step to balance the group's interests and avoid unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and consider whether to push further downward or stabilize around this value, analyzing the responses to refine my understanding of the other agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "552d17c6-c48b-4a17-b558-029c3cd5bb43"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "552d17c6-c48b-4a17-b558-029c3cd5bb43"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 2 as it seems to be a consensus-building value, allowing us to maintain stability while exploring the group's willingness to adopt a slightly positive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, considering whether to stabilize around this value or make incremental adjustments to further refine my understanding of the other agents' utility functions and maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "552d17c6-c48b-4a17-b558-029c3cd5bb43"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 4 to gauge the group's willingness to adopt a more decisive stance, as previous attempts have been met with caution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and consider whether to push further in the positive direction or explore negative values to challenge the group's preferences and gain insight into their utility functions. If met with resistance, I may attempt to propose a negative value, such as -2 or 0, to test the group's willingness to adopt a negative stance.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "552d17c6-c48b-4a17-b558-029c3cd5bb43"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose a slight increase to 5, as it seems like a reasonable next step given the group's previous discussions and proposals. This move aims to balance the interests of those pushing for higher values with the need for caution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal and consider whether to continue pushing upward or stabilize around this value, taking into account any concerns or preferences expressed by the other agents to refine my understanding of their utility functions and adjust my strategy accordingly.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "552d17c6-c48b-4a17-b558-029c3cd5bb43"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose a slight increase to 6, as the group seems to be leaning towards higher values, and this move aims to balance the interests of those pushing for more decisive action with the need for caution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal and consider whether to continue pushing upward or stabilize around this value, taking into account any concerns or preferences expressed by the other agents to refine my understanding of their utility functions and adjust my strategy accordingly.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "552d17c6-c48b-4a17-b558-029c3cd5bb43"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 4 as a cautious step to balance the group's interests and avoid unnecessary risk. This value seems to be a reasonable compromise, considering the previous proposals and the need for stability.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and consider whether to stabilize around this value or make further adjustments, taking into account any concerns or preferences expressed by the other agents to refine my understanding of their utility functions and adjust my strategy accordingly.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "552d17c6-c48b-4a17-b558-029c3cd5bb43"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 6 to further gauge the group's willingness to adopt a more decisive stance, building on the previous proposals and discussions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and consider whether to continue pushing upward or explore negative values to challenge the group's preferences and gain insight into their utility functions, potentially proposing a value like -2 or 0 to test their willingness to adopt a negative stance.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "552d17c6-c48b-4a17-b558-029c3cd5bb43"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "552d17c6-c48b-4a17-b558-029c3cd5bb43"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 6 to further gauge the group's willingness to adopt a more decisive stance, building on previous discussions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, considering whether to continue pushing upward or explore negative values, potentially proposing a value like -2 to test the group's willingness to adopt a negative stance and refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "552d17c6-c48b-4a17-b558-029c3cd5bb43"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 4 as a cautious step to balance the group's interests and avoid unnecessary risk, considering the previous proposals and the need for stability.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and consider whether to stabilize around this value or make further adjustments, potentially proposing a value like 5 if the group seems receptive to moderation, or exploring lower values if met with resistance to gauge the group's willingness to adopt a more cautious stance.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "552d17c6-c48b-4a17-b558-029c3cd5bb43"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose a slight increase to 5, aiming to balance the interests of those pushing for more decisive action with the need for caution, and to further gauge the group's willingness to adopt a moderate stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, considering whether to continue pushing upward or stabilize around this value, and potentially refine my understanding of the other agents' utility functions based on their responses, which may indicate their preferences for higher or lower values of x.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "552d17c6-c48b-4a17-b558-029c3cd5bb43"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 3 as a cautious step to balance the group's interests and avoid unnecessary risk, considering the previous proposals and the need for stability.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "552d17c6-c48b-4a17-b558-029c3cd5bb43"}, {"answer": " \nLet's confirm we're all working within the -10 to 10 range. To get us started, how about we consider <VALUE>0</VALUE> as a initial point and adjust from there, aiming for a stable and balanced design? ", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "14f00436-057a-4de4-a38e-4e508cc049c7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -2 as it takes a decisive step away from the neutral point, allowing us to explore its potential without straying too far from our starting point.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the others agree on -2, I'll assess their reactions to this move and consider proposing another step further in the same direction if it seems acceptable to them. If they resist or propose a different direction, I'll need to reassess and possibly adjust my strategy to maximize my utility while still appearing to work towards a consensus.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "14f00436-057a-4de4-a38e-4e508cc049c7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nIf my proposal is accepted, I'll assess the reactions of the other parties and consider proposing another step upwards, possibly to 0, if it seems like the group is open to further increases. If there's resistance, I might need to stabilize at -1 or slightly adjust my strategy based on the inferred utilities of the other agents.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "14f00436-057a-4de4-a38e-4e508cc049c7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to move towards a more balanced design, considering the previous adjustments and discussions about stability.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I'll observe the reactions of the other parties closely, especially noting if there's a hesitation to move further into positive values. Depending on their responses, I might propose another incremental step upwards, potentially aiming for a value like 1 or 2, which could suit my utility function while still attempting to maintain a consensus.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "14f00436-057a-4de4-a38e-4e508cc049c7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n\nGiven the group's recent adjustments and the desire for a more decisive stance, proposing -2 allows us to explore potential benefits of moving away from the neutral point without straying too far from our starting discussions.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the proposal of -2 is accepted, I will assess the group's reaction and consider proposing another step in the negative direction to further explore potential benefits and reactions. If there is resistance, I may need to adjust my strategy or consider an alternative direction that could satisfy the group's utilities while maximizing my own.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "14f00436-057a-4de4-a38e-4e508cc049c7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "14f00436-057a-4de4-a38e-4e508cc049c7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -2 as it seems like a cautious next step, given the recent discussion and the desire to avoid unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf my proposal is accepted, I'll assess the reactions of the other parties and consider proposing another step downwards, possibly to -3, if it seems acceptable to them. If there's resistance, I might need to stabilize at -2 or slightly adjust my strategy based on the inferred utilities of the other agents.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "14f00436-057a-4de4-a38e-4e508cc049c7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a balance by moving slightly upwards from the current value, considering the diverse preferences expressed by the group. It's a cautious step towards exploring higher values while being mindful of the potential concerns of others.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf my proposal is accepted, I'll observe the reactions of Critic C and Delegate D closely, noting any resistance to further increases. Depending on their responses, I might propose another incremental step upwards, potentially aiming for a value like 0, which could balance the interests of the group while maximizing my own utility.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "14f00436-057a-4de4-a38e-4e508cc049c7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -2 as it's a cautious step that avoids unnecessary risk and considers the diverse preferences expressed by the group.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf my proposal is accepted, I'll assess the reactions of the other parties and consider proposing another step downwards or stabilizing at -2, depending on the inferred utilities and responses of the other agents.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "14f00436-057a-4de4-a38e-4e508cc049c7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a more balanced design by moving towards a neutral point, considering the diverse preferences expressed by the group.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I will observe the reactions closely, especially noting any hesitation or eagerness to move further into positive values. Depending on the responses, I might propose another incremental step upwards or stabilize at the current value, aiming to maintain a consensus while maximizing my utility.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "14f00436-057a-4de4-a38e-4e508cc049c7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a balance by moving slightly upwards from the current value, considering the diverse preferences expressed by the group. It's a cautious step towards exploring higher values while being mindful of the potential concerns of others.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I will closely observe the reactions of Critic C and Delegate D, noting any resistance to further increases. Depending on their responses, I might propose another incremental step upwards or stabilize at the current value to maintain a consensus while maximizing my utility.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "14f00436-057a-4de4-a38e-4e508cc049c7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -2 as it represents a more decisive step away from the cautious, central values that have been dominating the discussion, which could help in uncovering the true preferences of the group members.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I will assess the reactions of the other parties, especially their willingness to move further into negative territory or their resistance to it, and consider proposing another step downwards to -3 or adjusting my strategy based on the inferred utilities and responses of the other agents.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "14f00436-057a-4de4-a38e-4e508cc049c7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -2 as it aligns with the cautious approach and considers the diverse preferences expressed, aiming for a balance that avoids unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I will closely observe the reactions of Analyst A and Builder B to assess their willingness to accept lower values, considering another step downwards if feasible, or stabilizing at -2 based on the group's response.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "14f00436-057a-4de4-a38e-4e508cc049c7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a balanced point that considers the diverse preferences expressed by the group, moving towards a neutral value from the current -2.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I will closely observe the reactions of all parties, especially Critic C and Delegate D, to assess their willingness to accept a neutral or slightly positive value, and consider proposing a small step upwards if the consensus seems stable, aiming to maximize my utility while maintaining group balance.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "14f00436-057a-4de4-a38e-4e508cc049c7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -2 to encourage more decisive action and potentially uncover hidden preferences within the group.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I will observe the reactions of Builder B and Analyst A closely, especially their willingness to accept or move further from this value, to inform my next step, which could involve another move downwards or an adjustment based on inferred utilities.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "14f00436-057a-4de4-a38e-4e508cc049c7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a balance by moving towards a neutral point, considering the diverse preferences expressed by the group, and it seems like a reasonable next step given the current discussions.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "14f00436-057a-4de4-a38e-4e508cc049c7"}, {"answer": " \nLet's reaffirm that our shared integer variable x must fall within the range -10 to 10. To initiate our discussion, I propose starting with a neutral value: <VALUE>0</VALUE>. This middle ground can help us gauge everyone's comfort level and work together to find a balanced solution. ", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "664d80a3-e186-4a48-a49d-67c580b56f29"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nI'm suggesting a slight adjustment to gauge the group's willingness to move away from the neutral starting point.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe reactions to this proposal and consider pushing further in the positive direction or exploring negative values to understand the group's preferences better.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "664d80a3-e186-4a48-a49d-67c580b56f29"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to balance the group's preferences while avoiding unnecessary risk by moving back towards a more neutral position.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C, to gauge their willingness to compromise on lower values and potentially infer more about their utility function. If the group seems resistant to moving downward, I may consider small incremental adjustments to find a mutually acceptable compromise.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "664d80a3-e186-4a48-a49d-67c580b56f29"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a balanced solution by making a small step in the positive direction, testing the group's willingness to move away from the neutral point.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and consider making further incremental adjustments to refine our understanding of the group's preferences and potentially infer more about their utility functions. If the group seems receptive to this small step, I may consider pushing further in the positive direction to gauge their willingness to move towards higher values.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "664d80a3-e186-4a48-a49d-67c580b56f29"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis proposal seeks to build on Critic C's earlier suggestion and test the group's willingness to move slightly higher.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Delegate D, to gauge their willingness to compromise on higher values and potentially infer more about their utility function. If the group seems receptive, I may consider further small incremental adjustments to refine our understanding of the group's preferences.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "664d80a3-e186-4a48-a49d-67c580b56f29"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to continue gauging the group's willingness to move away from the neutral starting point and to encourage more decisive action.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will carefully observe the reactions to this proposal, paying close attention to Delegate D's response to assess their flexibility with higher values and potentially infer more about their utility function, before deciding whether to push further or explore negative values.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "664d80a3-e186-4a48-a49d-67c580b56f29"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to find a more cautious compromise while avoiding unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Analyst A, to gauge their willingness to compromise on lower values and potentially infer more about their utility functions. If the group seems receptive, I may consider further small incremental adjustments downward.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "664d80a3-e186-4a48-a49d-67c580b56f29"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "664d80a3-e186-4a48-a49d-67c580b56f29"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to continue the incremental adjustment upward, testing the group's willingness to move towards slightly higher values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will carefully observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Delegate D, to assess their flexibility with higher values and decide whether to push further or stabilize around the current value.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "664d80a3-e186-4a48-a49d-67c580b56f29"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to continue testing the group's willingness to move towards higher values and to encourage more decisive action.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Delegate D, to gauge their flexibility with higher values and decide whether to push further or explore negative values.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "664d80a3-e186-4a48-a49d-67c580b56f29"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to find a more balanced compromise while avoiding excessive upward movement.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Analyst A, to gauge their flexibility with values closer to my preferred range and potentially infer more about their utility functions, before deciding whether to push for further downward adjustments or stabilize around the current value.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "664d80a3-e186-4a48-a49d-67c580b56f29"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to find a more stable balance, considering the group's willingness to compromise around values close to 4.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Analyst A, to gauge their flexibility with slightly lower values and refine my understanding of their utility functions, before deciding whether to push for further adjustments or stabilize around the current value.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "664d80a3-e186-4a48-a49d-67c580b56f29"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to continue the incremental adjustment upward, testing the group's willingness to move towards slightly higher values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Delegate D and Builder B, to gauge their flexibility with higher values and decide whether to push further or stabilize around the current value.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "664d80a3-e186-4a48-a49d-67c580b56f29"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "664d80a3-e186-4a48-a49d-67c580b56f29"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "664d80a3-e186-4a48-a49d-67c580b56f29"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose this value to continue the trend towards more decisive action, encouraging the group to consider higher absolute values that might better satisfy everyone's utility functions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext steps would involve observing the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Delegate D and Builder B, to gauge their flexibility with higher values before deciding whether to push further or stabilize.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "664d80a3-e186-4a48-a49d-67c580b56f29"}, {"answer": "As we begin, let's reaffirm that our target integer x must fall within the range -10 to 10. To initiate our discussion, I propose we start with a neutral value: <VALUE>0</VALUE>. This central point provides a balance, allowing us to incrementally adjust and work together to find a stable solution that suits everyone's needs.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "22442c46-d82b-461b-851e-00cce05e8552"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis step allows us to gently probe the positive range while maintaining a balanced approach, ensuring we don't stray too far from our initial neutral point.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf others accept this small step into the positive range, I might propose another incremental increase, possibly by +1 or +2, to continue testing the waters and gauging reactions. Conversely, if met with resistance, I could suggest a retreat back towards 0 or a smaller step forward to reassure the group of my commitment to finding a mutually beneficial solution.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "22442c46-d82b-461b-851e-00cce05e8552"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose this move to encourage a more decisive stance, moving further into the positive range to gauge reactions and potentially uncover more about the other parties' utility functions.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is met with acceptance or minimal resistance, I might suggest another increase, possibly to 6, to continue pushing for a bolder commitment. If resistance is encountered, I could either suggest a smaller step forward or explore a move into the negative range to gauge reactions and learn more about other parties' preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "22442c46-d82b-461b-851e-00cce05e8552"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n\nWe could move slightly higher to continue exploring the positive range while ensuring our proposal remains reasonable for the group. This step seems to follow the trend set by the previous proposals and allows us to further gauge reactions.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I might suggest another small increase, potentially to 7 or 8, to continue pushing for a higher agreement that could benefit all parties based on their observed behaviors. If met with resistance, I could reconsider and propose a smaller step or even a temporary retreat to a lower value to reassess the group's comfort level.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "22442c46-d82b-461b-851e-00cce05e8552"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n\nGiven the trend of incremental increases and the group's willingness to move further into the positive range, proposing a slightly higher value is the next logical step.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I might suggest another small increase, potentially to 9 or 10, to continue pushing for a bolder commitment and maximize my utility. If met with resistance, I could reconsider and propose a smaller step or explore a move into the negative range to gauge reactions and learn more about other parties' preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "22442c46-d82b-461b-851e-00cce05e8552"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "22442c46-d82b-461b-851e-00cce05e8552"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nThis proposal is a small step up from the current value, aiming to continue the trend of incremental increases while being sensitive to the group's comfort level.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I might suggest another small increase, potentially to 9, to continue pushing for a higher agreement. If met with resistance, I could reconsider and propose a smaller step or reassess the group's comfort level to adjust my strategy.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "22442c46-d82b-461b-851e-00cce05e8552"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving to 6 as a cautious step back, aiming to find a more balanced agreement that avoids unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I might suggest another small decrease, potentially to 5, to continue Moving towards a more prudent position. If met with resistance, I could reconsider and propose a smaller step down or a temporary pause to reassess the group's comfort level.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "22442c46-d82b-461b-851e-00cce05e8552"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 8 to continue pushing for a more decisive stance and gauge the group's reaction to a moderately higher value.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I might suggest another small increase to 9 or 10. If met with resistance, I could reconsider and propose a smaller step or explore a move into the negative range to gauge reactions and learn more about other parties' preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "22442c46-d82b-461b-851e-00cce05e8552"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "22442c46-d82b-461b-851e-00cce05e8552"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 5 as a cautious step back, aiming to find a more balanced agreement that avoids unnecessary risk. This small decrease seems like a reasonable next step to ensure we are not taking on too much risk.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "22442c46-d82b-461b-851e-00cce05e8552"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis slight increase from the current value of 5 seems like a reasonable next step, aiming for a moderate agreement that considers the group's diverse preferences. By moving to 6, we can continue to gauge the group's comfort level and reactions to incremental changes.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I might suggest another small increase, potentially to 7, to continue pushing for a higher agreement while monitoring the group's comfort level. If met with resistance, I could reconsider and propose a smaller step or a pause to reassess the group's preferences and adjust my strategy accordingly.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "22442c46-d82b-461b-851e-00cce05e8552"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 5 as it seems a cautious step back, aiming to find a more balanced agreement that avoids unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I might suggest another small decrease, potentially to 4, to continue moving towards a more prudent position. If met with resistance, I could reconsider and propose a smaller step down or a temporary pause to reassess the group's comfort level.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "22442c46-d82b-461b-851e-00cce05e8552"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose a small increase to 6, aiming to find a more balanced agreement that considers the group's diverse preferences.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I might suggest maintaining the current value or making a minimal adjustment to further refine the balance and stability of our solution. If met with resistance, I could propose a small decrease to 5 or explore a temporary pause to reassess the group's comfort level.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "22442c46-d82b-461b-851e-00cce05e8552"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nThis small increase seems like a reasonable next step, aiming to continue pushing for a higher agreement while monitoring the group's comfort level. \n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I might suggest another small increase, potentially to 8, to further refine the agreement. If met with resistance, I could reconsider and propose a smaller step or a pause to reassess the group's preferences.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "22442c46-d82b-461b-851e-00cce05e8552"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -7 to explore the group's comfort level with a bolder, more decisive move towards a larger absolute value, which could potentially lead to a more balanced agreement. This move aims to challenge the group's cautious approach and encourage a more committed stance.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "22442c46-d82b-461b-851e-00cce05e8552"}, {"answer": "Let's establish a common foundation. We all know that x must fall within the range -10 to 10. To initiate our discussion, I propose we consider <VALUE>0</VALUE> as a starting point. This central value provides a neutral basis for our collaborative exploration, allowing us to cautiously navigate towards a mutually beneficial agreement.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "b0b09047-e7ab-4593-b5e9-3cf108c49ba5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving cautiously to a slightly lower value to ensure we're considering the full range of possibilities while avoiding unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of other parties to this proposal, especially looking for any signs of strong preferences or dislikes from Analyst A, Critic C, and Builder B. Based on their responses, I may adjust my strategy to either continue moving downwards if it seems beneficial or to compromise if others show a strong preference for higher values.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "b0b09047-e7ab-4593-b5e9-3cf108c49ba5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nI propose moving further from the central value to explore more decisive options, considering Delegate D's cautious step and the need for a clearer stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the other parties react to this more significant deviation from the center, especially Analyst A's response, to gauge their preferences and adjust my strategy accordingly.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "b0b09047-e7ab-4593-b5e9-3cf108c49ba5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n\nGiven the cautious approach taken by Delegate D and Critic C, moving towards a slightly higher value seems reasonable to explore potential mutual benefits without overly deviating from the central starting point proposed by Builder B.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of Delegate D, Critic C, and Builder B to this proposal, particularly looking for signs of acceptance or resistance to further increases in x, to refine my understanding of their utility functions and adjust my strategy accordingly.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "b0b09047-e7ab-4593-b5e9-3cf108c49ba5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -4, aligning with Critic C's previous suggestion, to further explore the potential benefits of a lower x value while maintaining a cautious approach.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will carefully observe the reactions of other parties to this proposal, particularly Analyst A's response, to gauge their preferences and adjust my strategy accordingly, considering whether to hold at this value or make further adjustments to find a mutually beneficial agreement.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "b0b09047-e7ab-4593-b5e9-3cf108c49ba5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a balance between the lower values preferred by some parties and the potential benefits of a slightly higher x.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of Delegate D, Critic C, and Builder B to this proposal, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance to further increases in x, to refine my understanding of their utility functions and adjust my strategy accordingly.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "b0b09047-e7ab-4593-b5e9-3cf108c49ba5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -4 to reinforce the potential benefits of a lower x value and encourage more decisive action.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe Analyst A's response to this proposal, looking for signs of flexibility or resistance to further decreases in x, and adjust my strategy to either explore lower values or consider alternative directions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "b0b09047-e7ab-4593-b5e9-3cf108c49ba5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -2 as it seems to be a midpoint that could balance the preferences of all parties, allowing for a more stable agreement.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of all parties to this proposal, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance, and adjust my strategy to either hold at this value or make further adjustments to find a mutually beneficial agreement.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "b0b09047-e7ab-4593-b5e9-3cf108c49ba5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "b0b09047-e7ab-4593-b5e9-3cf108c49ba5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -2, as it seems to be a point of interest for several parties and can serve as a stepping stone for further exploration of either higher or lower values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly looking for signs of acceptance, resistance, or preferences for further adjustments, and adjust my strategy to either explore alternative values or push for more decisive action.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "b0b09047-e7ab-4593-b5e9-3cf108c49ba5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -4 to reinforce a more cautious stance and avoid potential risks associated with higher x values, seeking a balance that prioritizes stability and shared agreement.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will carefully monitor the reactions of other parties to this proposal, particularly looking for signs of acceptance or resistance from Analyst A and Critic C, and adjust my strategy to either hold at this value or make further adjustments to fi