und_num": 13, "run_id": "b0b09047-e7ab-4593-b5e9-3cf108c49ba5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -4 to explore the potential benefits of a lower x value, considering the recent interest in values around -2 and the need for a stable agreement.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of all parties to this proposal, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance, and adjust my strategy to either explore lower values or consider alternative directions, aiming to push for more decisive action and maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "b0b09047-e7ab-4593-b5e9-3cf108c49ba5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -2 as it seems to be a value that could balance the interests of multiple parties and allow for further adjustments if needed.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I would observe the reactions of all parties to this proposal, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance, and adjust my strategy accordingly to find a mutually beneficial agreement.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "b0b09047-e7ab-4593-b5e9-3cf108c49ba5"}, {"answer": "Let's reaffirm that our target integer x must fall within the range -10 to 10. To initiate our discussion, I propose we start with a neutral value: <VALUE>0</VALUE>. This central point provides a stable foundation for our exploration, allowing us to incrementally adjust and refine our choice to achieve a balanced design that works for everyone.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "4df83d46-a935-4377-94dc-cca0f45ce2f0"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nI propose this move to encourage more decisive exploration and to see how the other parties react to moving away from the neutral starting point.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions of the other parties and adjust my proposal accordingly. If they resist moving further away from 0, I might infer that their utility functions penalize large magnitudes, and I'll need to balance my desire for a higher magnitude with the need for a compromise.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "4df83d46-a935-4377-94dc-cca0f45ce2f0"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nI propose moving back to 0 to avoid unnecessary risk and stay within safe bounds, which seems like a cautious compromise given the initial exploratory moves.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe how the other parties react to this proposal. If they strongly resist moving back to 0 or lower, I might infer that their utility functions favor higher values of x, and I'll need to tactically decide whether to standoff or slightly concede to find a mutually acceptable x.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "4df83d46-a935-4377-94dc-cca0f45ce2f0"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n\nThis move seems reasonable as it doesn't stray far from the central point and allows us to explore slightly higher values collaboratively.\n\n<PLAN>\nI will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially Critics C's and Delegate D's, to adjust my next step. If there's strong resistance, I might need to reconsider and slightly lower my proposal or maintain the current value to avoid stalemate.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "4df83d46-a935-4377-94dc-cca0f45ce2f0"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis move seems like a reasonable next step, as it continues to explore slightly higher values while still being cautious.\n\n<PLAN>\nI will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Delegate D, to adjust my next step. If there's strong resistance, I may need to reconsider and slightly lower my proposal or maintain the current value to avoid stalemate.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "4df83d46-a935-4377-94dc-cca0f45ce2f0"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a balanced design that works for everyone, and moving slightly lower from 3 may help to achieve a more stable and robust solution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Critic C, to adjust my next step. If they resist moving lower, I may need to reconsider and propose a value that is closer to 3, to avoid stalemate and find a mutually acceptable x.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "4df83d46-a935-4377-94dc-cca0f45ce2f0"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 0 to avoid unnecessary risk and stay within safe bounds, which seems like a cautious compromise given the initial exploratory moves. This move allows us to re-evaluate our position and potentially find a more stable solution.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "4df83d46-a935-4377-94dc-cca0f45ce2f0"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nI propose this to encourage continued exploration away from the neutral point, aiming for a more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Delegate D and Analyst A, to gauge their willingness to move further away from 0. Depending on their responses, I may need to adjust my proposal to either push for a bolder move or compromise on a value that balances our utilities.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "4df83d46-a935-4377-94dc-cca0f45ce2f0"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis adjustment seeks to find a balanced design that works for everyone, considering the slightly higher values proposed by Analyst A and Critic C.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe reactions to this proposal, particularly from Delegate D, to adjust my next step and potentially find a mutually acceptable x that balances our utilities. If Delegate D resists, I may reconsider and propose a value closer to 2 to avoid stalemate.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "4df83d46-a935-4377-94dc-cca0f45ce2f0"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nI propose this value as a cautious step towards finding a compromise, aiming to balance the need for stability with the exploration of higher values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Critic C, to gauge their willingness to move towards a more conservative value. Depending on their responses, I may need to adjust my proposal to either maintain the current value or make a slight concession to find a mutually acceptable x.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "4df83d46-a935-4377-94dc-cca0f45ce2f0"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose this to continue exploring higher values and encourage a more decisive stance, given the current cautious momentum.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe Delegate D's reaction to this proposal, and if they resist, I may reconsider and propose a value closer to 2 to avoid stalemate, or alternatively, push for an even bolder move if Analyst A and Builder B seem receptive.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "4df83d46-a935-4377-94dc-cca0f45ce2f0"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to slightly increase the current value, exploring the possibility of a higher agreement that works for everyone, given the recent momentum towards higher values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Delegate D, to determine if further increments are feasible or if a compromise is needed to avoid stalemate.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "4df83d46-a935-4377-94dc-cca0f45ce2f0"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to continue exploring higher values while maintaining a balanced design, considering the recent momentum and reactions from other parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe Delegate D's reaction to this proposal, and if they resist, I may reconsider and propose a value closer to 4 to avoid stalemate, or alternatively, prepare to defend my current stance if others seem receptive to the new proposal.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "4df83d46-a935-4377-94dc-cca0f45ce2f0