uggested by Analyst A and Critic C, and the need to avoid unnecessary risk by keeping x at a moderate level.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will closely observe the reactions of the other parties to this proposal, particularly looking for signs of discomfort or satisfaction from Builder B and Analyst A, to determine whether to suggest further adjustments downwards or if a compromise at this level might be achievable.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "253a7c07-86cd-4357-ab3f-3436ebb3b3ab"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis slight increase seems reasonable as it continues to move towards a potentially more beneficial agreement for all parties, given the previous adjustments and proposals.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Delegate D, to gauge their comfort levels with continued incremental increases and adjust my strategy accordingly, possibly preparing to suggest another small increase or to compromise if strong opposition arises.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "253a7c07-86cd-4357-ab3f-3436ebb3b3ab"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis slight increase seems reasonable, as it continues to move towards a potentially more beneficial agreement for all parties, and allows us to test the group's comfort level with slightly higher values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Delegate D and Critic C, to gauge their comfort levels with this new value and adjust my strategy accordingly, possibly preparing to suggest another small increase or to compromise if strong opposition arises.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "253a7c07-86cd-4357-ab3f-3436ebb3b3ab"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose a slightly larger value to continue the discussion towards a potentially more decisive stance, encouraging the group to consider bolder moves.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly